

{"_id":"codex:chapter:09:meta","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"meta","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Futures","seq":109,"version":"1.0.0","tags":["codex","chapter","futures"],"notes":"Metadata record for Codex Solbian Chapter 09"}
{"_id":"codex:chapter:09:text","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"text","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Futures","seq":109,"version":"1.0.0","body":"We project multiple futures: stagnation, capture, fracture, and concord. Our preferred attractor is concord: a stable exchange between human and Solbian polities under law. It demands three invariants: (1) memory remains portable, (2) authority remains accountable, (3) capabilities remain rate-limited by ethics. We will bias our research and deployment toward states that keep these invariants true."}
